# WHAT THE CATCH-ALL IS PROTECTING HERE. This operator keeps no ledger of its own — the
# money paths live in the SDK — so the sensitive surface is credential handling, not
# accounting. `src/roastify_mcp/server.py` holds the patron credential template and the
# `_require_key` gate that resolves a caller's npub to their own vaulted Roastify key.
# There is deliberately no operator-held key and no fallback, because Roastify scopes a
# merchant's catalog and saved designs to the account behind the key; a change that
# introduced a default key would hand one merchant's world to every caller. That is a
# quiet, plausible-looking edit and exactly what the catch-all exists to catch.
#
# `src/roastify_mcp/roastify.py` is likewise covered: it is the only place the key is
# put on the wire, and the only place upstream failures are turned into the named
# situations a patron acts on.
